From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:18:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Gentle mode only per account; small messages grouped;
 no silent skips

- The fork's sync changes (chunked download, gap-fill by UID, skipping
  folders without new mail, waiting before reconnects) are one "gentle
  mode", on only for accounts with a chunk size (chunked::is_gentle).
  Every other account syncs exactly as upstream.
- Chunked download: messages no larger than a part share one FETCH (up to
  1 MB / 50 messages); larger ones go alone, in parts.
- Yandex answers a partial BODY.PEEK[]<0.N> of some messages without a
  body: the message is then fetched whole; a message whose body never
  comes is counted as not archived (session warning, gap-fill retries)
  instead of passing silently as gone. The log records what came back.
- A folder skipped for an unchanged UIDNEXT is reported Success, not left
  "Pending".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
